  "body": "# CoAkka Runtime 1.4.1 Corrective Release\n\nRuntime `1.4.1` replaces the incomplete native platform coverage of\n`1.4.0+2cee86bf`. The release is built from full core source commit\n`9e02a51d7f0e4a231e2f71fe6d19ce02724277c9`.\n\n## Corrected Boundary\n\nThe native package, `coakka-client`, and `coakka-runtime-inspect` each contain\nexactly these five platforms:\n\n- Linux ARM64\n- Linux x86-64\n- macOS ARM64\n- Windows ARM64\n- Windows x86-64\n\nThe native package is\n`runtime/native/releases/1.4.1+9e02a51d/coakka-runtime-native-v2-1.4.1.tar.gz`\nwith SHA-256\n`ef31cd8bc709bd71d62dab0497f2513990f9023bda5e128631842ece5360394f`.\nIts manifest and checksum file are authoritative for the platform entries.\n\n## Connector And Tool Identity\n\n- JVM, Spring Boot, and Quarkus: `1.4.1-g9e02a51d-4e7cda4`\n- Source connector artifacts: `1.4.1+9e02a51d-4e7cda4`\n- Node.js, Bun, and Electron packages: `1.4.6`, source `37816322`\n- NuGet package: `CoAkka.Runtime` `1.4.7`, source `af244b1e`\n- Python PyPI package: `coakka-v2-connector` `1.4.6`, source `603a3728`\n- Native tools: `1.4.1+9e02a51d`\n\nThe Python, NuGet, and npm packages are registry-verified. The NuGet.org\ndownload contains the exact staged entries plus its repository signature. npm\nserves the exact Node.js, Bun, and Electron `1.4.6` versions under the\n`latest` dist-tag.\n\n## Verification Gates\n\n- All five native libraries pass binary-format, architecture, dependency, and\n  exact-export checks.\n- Linux ARM64/x86-64 and macOS ARM64 execute on matching hosts.\n- Windows ARM64 executes on Windows 11 ARM64: runtime lifecycle, JVM\n  ask/deadletter, `coakka-client` version/doctor, and\n  `coakka-runtime-inspect` command smokes pass.\n- `coakka-client` and `coakka-runtime-inspect` archives pass per-platform\n  format, checksum, and dependency verification.\n- Linux `coakka-runtime-inspect serve` HTTP smokes pass on both architectures.\n- `coakka-runtime-inspect` keeps libuv as a private static tool dependency.\n  The Windows resolver rejects `libuv.dll.a`, and release dependency gates\n  reject dynamic libuv or protobuf dependencies.\n- The publish manifest, native linkage, public-surface scanner, and JVM native\n  bundle gates pass before registry publication.\n\n## Publication Rule\n\nNo `current` pointer or package-manager status is advanced from candidate to\ncurrent until the registry returns the exact published version and digest.",
